jobs.description:
Do you enjoy working on complex technology where different systems have to work together perfectly?


Are you an experienced engineer with a background in electronics, systems engineering, embedded systems, RF or electrical engineering? And would you like to contribute to a unique, long-term R&D project?


For a high-tech R&D project in Mol, Belgium, we are looking for a Senior Electronics & Systems Engineer to support the development, integration and commissioning of electronics for a new superconducting linear accelerator.


You do not necessarily need previous experience with particle accelerators. We are particularly interested in engineers with a strong background in LLRF, systems engineering, embedded electronics or electrical/electronics engineering, combined with experience in complex R&D environments.


Your role



• You will join a multidisciplinary engineering team responsible for the electronics supporting the accelerator.

• Your role will be broad: you will work on the development of electronic systems, help integrate different technical subsystems and make sure that these systems work together as one reliable and well-functioning solution. 


Your responsibilities will include:



• Supporting the engineering, integration and commissioning of electronic systems;

• Contributing to systems related to Low-Level RF (LLRF) and beam diagnostics;

• Translating technical needs into clear requirements, technical specifications and acceptance criteria;

• Supporting system architecture and the definition of complex technical systems;

• Supporting the integration and verification of different subsystems;

• Developing and testing simulation models and prototypes to validate technical concepts;

• Contributing to the development and verification of embedded electronics, FPGA and firmware;

• Supporting the setup and management of dedicated test facilities where different systems are brought together;

• Supporting installation, testing, commissioning and verification activities;

• Maintaining technical documentation throughout the full lifecycle of the systems;

• Working closely with internal teams, international partners and external suppliers;

• Supporting technical procurement processes and supplier follow-up. 


In short: you help develop complex electronic systems and make sure that all the different technical pieces work together as one system.

Your background


We are looking for a senior engineer with a broad technical perspective. You do not need to have every skill listed below. A strong background in one or more of these areas is particularly relevant:


LLRF / RF



• Experience with Low-Level RF systems;

• Experience with RF electronics or RF control systems;

• Experience with accelerator technology is a strong asset. 


Systems Engineering



• Experience with system architecture, requirements and technical specifications;

• Experience with system integration, verification and testing;

• Comfortable working across different technical subsystems and disciplines. 


Embedded / Electronics



• Experience with embedded systems engineering;

• Experience with electronics, FPGA and/or firmware;

• Knowledge of programming languages such as Python, C or C++. 


Electrical / Electronics Engineering



• A strong background in electrical engineering, electronics or a related discipline;

• Experience developing or integrating complex technical systems in an industrial or research-oriented R&D environment. 


In addition, you:



• hold a Master's degree or PhD in Electrical Engineering, Electronics, Physics or a related technical field or equivalent by experience; 

• are comfortable working independently and taking initiative;

• can switch easily between different technical topics, priorities and requirements;

• communicate clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders;

• have excellent written and spoken English. 


Nice to haves:



• Experience with procurement, supplier follow-up, collaborative projects or dedicated test facilities 

• Knowledge of Dutch and/or French
